{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.CategoricalLinkingOperation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.CategoricalLinkingOperation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Prod","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Prod","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.no_global_instance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.no_global_instance","kind":"theorem","line":353,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L353-L360","doc":"**Corollary: no global instance exists.**  A `CategoricalLinkingOperation`\nfor every `LinkingData` would in particular give one for\n`counterexampleData`, contradicting `postTraceMultiplicative_fails`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.postTraceMultiplicative_fails","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.postTraceMultiplicative_fails","kind":"theorem","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L339-L351","doc":"**The `postTraceMultiplicative` field is falsifiable** — it fails for\n`counterexampleData` at `k₁ = 0`, `k₂ = 1`, `a = (1,1)`, `b = (1,0)`:\nthe left side is `(2, 2)` and the right side is `(2, 3)`.  So\n`CategoricalLinkingOperation` is not satisfied by every\n`LinkingData`, which is what the removed global `instance canonical`\nasserted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.counterexampleData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.counterexampleData","kind":"def","line":331,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L331-L337","doc":"Counterexample data over `ℚ × ℚ`: trace `(x, y) ↦ x + y`, braiding\n`c = (2, 3)`, dual and bar the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.lk_bar_trace_cut_compose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.lk_bar_trace_cut_compose","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L312-L321","doc":"**Conditional consequence (§3b-cond).**  *If* the conjecture holds,\nthe trace-cut symmetry and the bar compatibility compose into the\nself-conjugacy statement `ι(Lk^{(-k)}(b,a)) = Lk^{(-k)}(ι a, ι b)` —\nderived from two fields, not read off one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.CategoricalLinkingOperation.barCompatible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.CategoricalLinkingOperation.barCompatible","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L309-L309","doc":"Property 5: `ι(Lk^{(k)}(a,b)) = Lk^{(-k)}(ι a, ι b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.CategoricalLinkingOperation.traceCutSymmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.CategoricalLinkingOperation.traceCutSymmetric","kind":"theorem","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L306-L306","doc":"Property 4: `Lk^{(k)}(a,b) = ι(Lk^{(-k)}(b,a))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.CategoricalLinkingOperation.postTraceMultiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.CategoricalLinkingOperation.postTraceMultiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L303-L303","doc":"Property 3, post-trace: `Lk^{(k₁+k₂)}(a,b) = c^{k₂} · Lk^{(k₁)}(a,b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.CategoricalLinkingOperation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.CategoricalLinkingOperation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L299-L299","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.CategoricalLinkingOperation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.CategoricalLinkingOperation","kind":"class","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L268-L310","doc":"**Conjecture carrier (primary, content-bearing, NO instance).**\n`CategoricalLinkingOperation R A D` asserts the three properties of\n`conj:categorical-linking-operation` that are *not* generic:\n\n* `postTraceMultiplicative` — Property 3 **after** the trace cut.  The\n  pre-trace statement is `preLk_add` above and is proved; lifting it\n  through `τ_R` needs the substrate commutation identity\n  `τ_R(c^{k₂} · x) = c^{k₂} · τ_R(x)`-in-the-relevant-sense, which the\n  `.md` does not supply.  `postTraceMultiplicative_fails` below\n  exhibits data for which this field is **false**, so it is a genuine\n  constraint.\n* `traceCutSymmetric` — Property 4: cutting the other component\n  produces the `ι`-conjugate with reversed linking sign.  Conditional\n  on Markov-trace cyclicity (whose half is proved above as\n  `trace_cut_cyclicity_step`) *and* ribbon braiding inversion\n  `ι(c) = c⁻¹`, which is not part of `LinkingData`.\n* `barCompatible` — Property 5: `ι(Lk^{(k)}(a,b)) = Lk^{(-k)}(ι a, ι b)`,\n  conditional on bar-functoriality of `c` and `τ_R`.\n\nProperties 1 and 2 are **not** fields: they are proved unconditionally\nabove (`lk_bilinear`, `lk_zero`), so carrying them as hypotheses would\noverstate what is open.\n\n**Tower status (owner ruling 2026-09-03): ORDER-ZERO-ONLY.**  The\noperation is stated at a single fixed substrate `A`; the `H_n(q)` tower\nis not used.\n\nNo instance is provided; supplying one asserts the conjecture. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:categorical-linking-operation","label":"conj:categorical-linking-operation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.preLk_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.preLk_add","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L255-L264","doc":"**Property 3, pre-trace half (PROVED):** additional linkings are\npre-composition with `c_{A,A}`,\n`PreLk^{(k₁+k₂)}(a, b) = c^{k₂} · PreLk^{(k₁)}(a, b)`, by\n`zpow_add` in the group `Aˣ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.lk_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.lk_zero","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L239-L246","doc":"**Property 2 (`.md`), proved:** `Lk_R^{(0)}(a, b) = τ_R(b) · a^*`.\nThe previous revision \"proved\" this as `q ^ (0 : ℕ) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.lk_bilinear","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.lk_bilinear","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L229-L235","doc":"**Property 1 (`.md`), proved: `Lk_R^{(k)}` is `R`-bilinear.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.lk_smul_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.lk_smul_right","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L223-L227","doc":"`Lk_R^{(k)}(a, −)` is `R`-homogeneous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.lk_add_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.lk_add_right","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L217-L221","doc":"`Lk_R^{(k)}(a, −)` is additive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.lk_smul_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.lk_smul_left","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L211-L215","doc":"`Lk_R^{(k)}(−, b)` is `R`-homogeneous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.lk_add_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.lk_add_left","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L203-L209","doc":"`Lk_R^{(k)}(−, b)` is additive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LinkingData.lk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LinkingData.lk","kind":"def","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L180-L189","doc":"**The categorical linking operation** `Lk_R^{(k)}(a, b)` of the `.md`:\nclose the second component through the Frobenius trace after linking\nit to the first by `k` braidings, leaving the first as the free\nendomorphism `a^*`:\n\n    Lk_R^{(k)}(a, b) = τ_R(c^k · b) · a^*.\n\nAt `k = 0` this is the `.md`'s Property 2 verbatim\n(`Lk_R^{(0)}(a, b) = τ_R(b) · a^*`) — see `lk_zero`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LinkingData.preLk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LinkingData.preLk","kind":"def","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L176-L178","doc":"**The pre-trace morphism** `PreLk_R^{(k)}(a, b) := c_{A,A}^k ∘ (a ⊗ b)`\nof `categorical-linking-operation.md` §\"Proof of Property 3\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LinkingData.bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LinkingData.bar","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L170-L170","doc":"The bar involution `ι`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LinkingData.dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LinkingData.dual","kind":"def","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L168-L168","doc":"The rigid dual `a ↦ a^*`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LinkingData.c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LinkingData.c","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L166-L166","doc":"The braiding `c_{A,A}`, as a unit (so `c ^ (k : ℤ)` exists). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LinkingData.tau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LinkingData.tau","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L164-L164","doc":"The Frobenius trace `τ_R : A →ₗ[R] R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LinkingData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LinkingData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L162-L162","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LinkingData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LinkingData","kind":"structure","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L147-L170","doc":"**The data the `.md`'s linking operation is built from.**  An\n`R`-algebra `A` (intended: the Frobenius–Hopf substrate, `H_n(q)`\ninside `End_R(V^{⊗n})`) together with\n\n* `tau` — the Frobenius trace `τ_R : A →ₗ[R] R`;\n* `c` — the braiding `c_{A,A}` as a **unit** of `A`, which is what\n  makes the integer power `c^k` for `k : ℤ` (the linking index)\n  available at all;\n* `dual` — the rigid dual `a ↦ a^*`, an `R`-linear map;\n* `bar` — the bar involution `ι` (the Hecke antipode\n  `ι(σ_i) = σ_i^{-1}` at the substrate level).\n\nThe structure only *names* the data; which of its inhabitants are\nthe ribbon-categorical ones is what the conjecture class below\nasserts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trace_cut_cyclicity_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trace_cut_cyclicity_step","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L126-L143","doc":"**Conditional trace-cut substitution lemma (sorry-free).** Under\n`[MarkovTraceCyclic T R tr_M]`, the trace-cut transformation\nunderlying property 4 reduces (after strand-swap) to a single\napplication of the two-factor cyclicity identity:\n    `tr_M ((a * b) * c) = tr_M (c * (a * b))`.\nThe full trace-cut symmetry statement (with the `k → -k`\nexponent shift) requires *additionally* the ribbon-category\nbraiding-inversion identity `c⁻¹ = c̄`, which is downstream\nstructure not exposed in this Hecke-level lemma. The lemma\nhere records the cyclicity half of the discharge sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markov_trace_cyclic_three_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markov_trace_cyclic_three_factor","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L102-L124","doc":"**Three-factor cyclic rotation (sorry-free).** With `[Semigroup T]`\nproviding associativity, the two-factor Markov-trace swap lifts\nto the cyclic-rotation identity\n    `tr_M (A * B * C) = tr_M (B * C * A)`\nwhich is the structural shape `tr_M (c^{k_1} * X * c^{k_2}) =\ntr_M (c^{k_2} * c^{k_1} * X)` mentioned in the linking-operation\npost-trace discussion (with `A := c^{k_1}`, `B := X`,\n`C := c^{k_2}` and one extra application of the two-factor swap\non the inner factors). The Hecke-power group law lifts a\nconcrete `c^{k_1} * c^{k_2}` to `c^{k_1 + k_2}`; combined with\nthis rotation, that is the cyclicity half of the post-trace\nmultiplicativity step flagged as open in\n`categorical-linking-operation.md` §\"Proof of Property 3\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markov_trace_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markov_trace_swap","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L86-L100","doc":"**Two-factor Markov-trace swap (sorry-free, conditional on\n`MarkovTraceCyclic`).** Direct restatement of the class field\n`tr_cyclic`. The conclusion is exactly the two-factor swap,\nnot the full post-trace multiplicativity-in-`k` identity; the\nlatter follows from this swap *plus* the pre-trace integer-power\ngroup law of `c_{A,A}` and is captured by\n`markov_trace_cyclic_three_factor` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceCyclic.tr_cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceCyclic.tr_cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L84-L84","doc":"Cyclicity: `tr_M (A * B) = tr_M (B * A)` for all `A B : T`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceCyclic.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceCyclic.mk","kind":"ctor","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceCyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceCyclic","kind":"class","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-linking-operation.lean#L65-L84","doc":"**Markov-trace cyclicity (axiomatised typeclass).** A type-level\ncarrier `T` for the Markov trace `tr_M : T → R` together with the\ncyclicity identity `tr_M (A * B) = tr_M (B * A)` for all `A B : T`.\n\nThis is the categorical content of `prop:frobenius-gram-matrix`'s\nsymmetry clause: the Gram matrix `G_{ij} = tr_M (b_i * b_j)` is\nsymmetric *because of* Markov-trace cyclicity. The post-trace\ncyclicity rewrite below takes this class as an explicit hypothesis\n(§3b-cond conditional pattern); any concrete substrate\n`T = H_n(q)` satisfies `MarkovTraceCyclic` by the standard Markov-\nproperty argument (peel boundary generator from the right; cite\nprop:frobenius-gram-matrix §\"Markov trace of NF basis elements\").\n","signatureChunk":0}]}